<hick:user>Implement Sam's proposal from the meeting upstream of this document as code this document owns. (1) Paste, by reference, the meeting turn where Sam proposes the pool change (it is the fifth utterance) so the reader sees what was asked. (2) Add a hick:file at path fix/pool.py: a small Python module with DEFAULT_POOL_SIZE = 10, FIXED_POOL_SIZE = 40, ACQUIRE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS = 2.0 and a function pool_settings(env=os.environ) that returns {'size': 40, 'acquire_timeout': 2.0} when env CHECKOUT_POOL_FIX == '1' and {'size': 10, 'acquire_timeout': None} otherwise. (3) Add a hick:container (python:3.12), a hick:volume input='.', and a hick:exec cell that cds into the mounted fix/ directory and prints pool_settings({}) and then pool_settings() with CHECKOUT_POOL_FIX=1, pinned with hick:expect match=exact (the expected text starts right after the opening tag, no line break). (4) Under '## Findings' add two hick:copy fragments class=finding: id fix-summary (what the fix does, the sizes, the timeout, the flag) and id forty-is-safe (Sam's capacity reasoning from the meeting: forty per replica, three replicas, instance configured for two hundred). Run verify until it passes, keep prose short, then stop.</hick:user>
